    "summary": "Boston Garden ’82 delivers soaring 'Samson', heartfelt 'Baby Blue' and Brent’s piano spotlight",
    "review": "What unfolds at the Boston Garden on September 18, 1982 is a quintessential early‑’80s Dead night that still feels fresh. The band kicks off with a crisp Jack Straw → Sugaree segue that sets a bright tone, then rolls through a tight first set highlighted by a scorching West L.A. Fadeaway and a soulful Dupree’s Diamond Blues. The second set erupts on a blistering Samson & Delilah – Jerry “smoking the strings” while Phil drops a bass bomb that drives the groove. Brent Mydland gets his birthday tribute in full swing, laying down piano gems on Far From Me and an intimate encore of It’s All Over Now Baby Blue that showcases his tender touch. The show closes with a joyous One More Saturday Night, leaving the Garden humming long after the lights went out.",
